  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "Acid house's minimalist sound combined house music's ubiquitous programmed four-on-the-floor 4/4 beat with the electronic squelch sound produced by the Roland TB-303 electronic synthesizer-sequencer. The sound is commonly produced by raising the filter resonance and lowering the cutoff frequency of the synthesizer, along with programming the 303's accent, slide, and octave parameters, to create variation in otherwise simple bass patterns. \"Exploration of texture\" is preferred over melody; \"a refusal of the metaphysical priorities of western music discourse\"."
  },
